  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The machine file can state a new optional key, `tooling.max_tool_number`. It is the highest tool number that the control's tool table holds.\n- The machine reader and the raw post engine refuse a value that is not a whole number of 1 or more. The message names the key.\n- The key is an installation fact, the same as `tooling.tool_change`. The mirror carries it. Scripts read it as `machine.toolNumberMax`.\n- `fehlmann-picomax55.mch` states `\"max_tool_number\": 254`.\n- `heidenhain-klartext.cps` refuses a higher tool number with a script error.\n- `heidenhain.cps` refuses a higher tool number with a counted warning. It refuses a spindle speed above the machine maximum in the same way.\n- A machine without the key keeps the old behaviour. Klartext keeps its limit of 32767. DIN/ISO has no limit.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/4087-tool-table-max.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe Picomax tool table has 254 lines (MP 7260 = 254, and the programming manual p. 2-16). No machine fact carried this limit. The Klartext post accepted tool numbers up to 32767, and the DIN/ISO post accepted all tool numbers. A program with tool 255 posted, and then the control stopped it with an alarm.\n\n`tooling.number_of_tools` is a different fact. It counts the distinct tools in a changer (`check_tool_count`). It does not limit the tool number.\n\n## Tests\n\nReview fix head: `576ae80811ca4b404a6260eafed39472df348b27`.\nBase: current `upstream/main` at `12ea01a45eccfc5c4cd221834eeb7d3e0400f806`.\nThe merge base is `e4d57ee`.\n\nThe review requested these corrections:\n\n- Tool 254 must return `Ok`, have no warnings, and contain the expected tool call. The pin checks both posts with raw and mirrored machine data. Tool 255 still requires the named refusal.\n- Issue #4087 and this body now state `effort:high`. The post refusal falls under the safety floor. The issue label was read back after the change.\n\nPin: `heidenhain_posts_refuse_a_tool_number_above_the_machine_tool_table` in `crates/post/tests/machine_controller.rs`.\nThe tool calls are `T254 G17 S3500` and `TOOL CALL 254 Z S3500`.\nThe malformed machine fact pin remains `malformed_declared_facts_refuse_at_the_machine_reader_and_raw_engine`.\n\nMutation command:\n`cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-post --test machine_controller heidenhain_posts_refuse_a_tool_number_above_the_machine_tool_table -- --exact`.\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Throw an unrelated error for tool 254 in `heidenhain.cps` | Red: tool 254 must post; 1 failed |\n| Revert only the test fix while keeping that error probe | Green: confirms the old test accepted the error |\n| Restore the test; throw the same error only in `heidenhain-klartext.cps` | Red: tool 254 must post; 1 failed |\n| Restore both posts and the final test | Green: all 6 `machine_controller` tests passed |\n\nAll probes were removed. No production file changed in this review fix.\n\nChecks on the final head:\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` | Green: 341 steps; 0 failed; 0 stalled; 27.5 minutes |\n| `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` | Green: no warnings; 1 minute 6 seconds |\n| `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` | Green: 72 steps; 0 failed; 0 stalled; 53.2 minutes |\n\nThe quick gate passed 1,227 post tests and 1,707 app tests. It left 42 app tests ignored as declared.\nThe heavy gate passed 66 ignored tests in release mode. Its 72 steps include the cold release build.\nThe catalog and golden suites ran in full:\n\n- `example_catalog`: 43 passed in quick. Its 4 ignored cases passed in the heavy gate.\n- `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`: 1 passed each.\n- `golden_cl`: 34 passed; `conformance`: 7 passed; `solid_law_goldens`: 7 passed.\n- `recorded_streams`: 12 passed; `script_heidenhain`: 11 passed; `script_heidenhain_klartext`: 23 passed.\n- `klartext_builtin`: 3 passed; post `machine_controller`: 6 passed.\n\nBuild environment: `RUSTC_WRAPPER` was unset. `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1` disabled the compile cache.\nThe gates used `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6` and `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1`.\nEarlier interrupted runs are invalid; they did not complete. The complete quick run above used a clean tree on the final head.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The quick gate ran the example catalog, `golden_cl`, `conformance` and the recorded script suites of both Heidenhain posts. No golden file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The machine sheet and the machine editor do not show the new key. The app does not judge the key in its own validator (`crates/app/src/machine/validate.rs`). The reader refuses a bad value when the file loads.\n- Physical-machine and app GUI checks did not run. The app posts through the same mirror that the pin uses.\n- The change has no UI. Screenshots are not required.\n- No other machine file states the key.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #4114 changes `assets/posts/heidenhain.cps` and `assets/posts/heidenhain-klartext.cps`. It changes other functions: the manifest line and a new `manualChange`. It does not change `onToolChange`. This PR adds lines at the start of `onToolChange` in `heidenhain.cps`, near the comment that #4114 changes. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: The machine file can state the highest tool number of the tool table (`tooling.max_tool_number`); the Fehlmann Picomax 55 states 254, and both Heidenhain posts refuse a higher tool number by name.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4087\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
